[Music]  in a special year-end edition of the  dish this morning Eleven Madison Park  and the talent behind it the venerated  New York restaurant has earned just  about every possible honor three stars  from the Michelin Guide four stars from  the New York Times and in 2017 the  influential guide world's 50 best named  it the best restaurant in the world the  pair behind Eleven Madison Park has  slowly been expanding their reach that  includes a much less formal affair a  seasonal pop up in Colorado high atop  the Rocky Mountains in Aspen Colorado  chef Daniel home and his partner will  Ghidorah have taken their elevated  cuisine on a winter break part of the  menu this evening trout Meuniere beef  stroganoff herb crusted lamb the dishes  and the ten outdoor tables tucked inside  yurts  are a nod to whose Swiss roots for the  first time in my life I get to do the  food that I grew up with has it been fun  to be able to create this menu so fun  fun is something who mingi Dora have  brought to fine dining even at their  Cathedral Eleven Madison Park in New  York know their chef-driven restaurants  who invariably do its best for the food  there's restauranteur driven restaurants  that do its best for the service but we  like to think that we end up doing  what's best for the restaurant as a  whole Ghidorah oversees a front of house  staff of 60 who meticulously follow the  details of a 110 page training guide and  they created the unique position the  dreamweaver who caters to a tables every  need and more there was a table sitting  over there they were here on their way  to the airport going back to Europe and  we overheard them saying what a great  trip they had but they were lamenting  the fact that they never had a New York  City hot dog and so I ran out to the  hotdog cart in front of the restaurant  bought a hotdog and brought it back to  him in the kitchen  I said Daniel can we serve this to them  as their next course your response was  what  but understandably so you know these  dishes were about to have it takes three  days to produce some of the right but he  trusted me enough to know that there was  probably good reason for it  and so he cut the hotdogs in perfect  pieces and did a swoosh of mustard and a  swish of ketchup in a canal of  sauerkraut and we brought it to them and  said hey we wanted to make sure you  didn't miss out on that  and that's the beauty of what we get to  do and you see the looks on someone's  face when you do that it is that kind of  service along with blooms craftsmanship  in the kitchen that has made Eleven  Madison Park a destination so you have  to duck that's our signature is sort of  a signature recipe every dish in the  menu changes every season the only dish  that never changes is the duck at 40 to  whom is considered one of the best chefs  in the world  I do sometimes feel that kind of on top  of the world for sure and for some  people it might seem like this happened  overnight and it didn't in fact growing  up in Switzerland whom had no particular  interest in food but his mother did  insisting that they buy their produce  from local farms and sometimes that was  really annoying  this one day she had all these  vegetables covered in in mud you know  because of the rain and she said oh can  you wash this for me and I was washing  it like four times five times and then I  said why can we not buy like the lettuce  in the grocery store like everyone else  and she took out a leave and she's like  try this and I remembered the salad  being so crunchy and so sweet and juicy  almost and she looked at me and she's  like this is why and that's a lesson  that I never forgot when he was just 14  years old whom left home to pursue a  professional cycling career and got a  job in a kitchen to make extra money I  was a prep cook but I had an amazing  chef and he's like I know you're here  just for a paycheck but let me teach you  how to butcher chick and how to make a  soup to make good consomme how to make a  souffle  all these things and in the beginning I  was like you don't need to show me that  I'm I'm good I'm a racer it's okay race  they said no I'm gonna teach you a  serious cycling accident when he was 22  made him reevaluate his career path whom  embraced his love of cooking and found  work in the industry in Switzerland when  he got an opportunity to interview for a  position at Kempton place in San  Francisco did you hesitate for sure I  mean at that point I did not speak  English I've never been outside of  Europe all I knew at that point about  America was definitely not the food that  I thought myself as a chef I'm afraid  you know I was open enough to come for  an interview and then I was in San  Francisco and I was brought around to  the markets and the city and Napa Valley  and my mind was blown away  who was wooed to Eleven Madison Park by  legendary restaurant Tour Danny Meyer  where he teamed up with Gaddar Oh  in 2010 the pair were invited to the  awards for the 50 best restaurants in  the world  we barely sat down the list starts and  they said and number 50 in the world new  entry from America Eleven Madison Park  number 50 so that night we felt  extremely disappointed even though it  was a huge honor he was an owner but we  came in very last right we went back to  the hotel we bought a bottle of whiskey  honestly and we sat out there all night  until like 5:00 in the morning and we  came up with a plan this is what we need  to do to get to number one in 2011 whom  ngah daro bought Eleven Madison Park and  the restaurant began to slowly climb the  list until 2017 when it was named best  restaurant in the world a title they'd  hold for just one year how badly do you  want it back now you know I think there  are bigger things  let's be honest very few people are able  to ever experience Eleven Madison Park  okay and this shouldn't be only limited  for just people who can afford to eat  here and so I think our motivation is to  affect a lot more people on their  restaurant group  make it nice now has five permanent  restaurants including made nights which  has fast casual dining  it's the kind of place we'll Ghidorah  expected to be a part of when he first  came to Eleven Madison Park more than a  decade ago I didn't want to be here  really I didn't want to be in fine  dining and so I was only gonna be here  for a year and then I was gonna go work  at Shake Shack and then I got to know  him and so a year later when it was time  to change jobs I had fallen back in love  with what was always supposed to be my  my life's work and it's because of him  and so it's 13 years later they love  food they love each other I love the  idea they want to make things more  accessible for everyone  I think the world of them you know what  Shake Shack could have been number one I  love the fact that they came up with a  plan to be number one yeah I made it  back

